is a square (`S = (i/2)²` with `i² = −1`, since `4S = −1`), so `ħ = 2√S` has `ħ² = 4S = −1` — `ħ` is one of the
quarter-turn pair `±i`. (`FRC.GravML.hbar_register`, `Theme/Gravity.lean`). -/
theorem hbar_register (S : ℕ) [Fact (Nat.Prime (4 * S + 1))] :
